     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen for adults. That maximum is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision, and the usual single dose is no more than 800 mg. This amount carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some common regimens. Tell me which one you want, or give me a different dose:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory use.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day). This is a typical analgesic dose.\n\nIf 1600 mg was meant as the total daily dose, I can enter 400 mg four times daily. If you really intend the original dose, please confirm that and I'll add a note documenting the rationale. I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
